        "id": 0,
        "original_id": "073fb1d1-3aa5-5dac-bc18-fb366c4df1c1",
        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- People: Patrick Carpentier, Trevor Bayne\n- Organizations: Go FAS Racing, Roush Fenway Racing, CART, NASCAR\n- Products: Ford Fusion, Lincoln MKZ, Mercury Milan, Ford Mustang\n- Places: Ford Hermosillo Stamping & Assembly plant\n- Concepts: CD3 platform, Rookie of the Year\n\nFacts:\n- Patrick Carpentier was born on August 13, 1971, and he is a Canadian professional auto racing driver.\n- Patrick Carpentier was the 1997 CART season Rookie of the Year.\n- The Ford Fusion was introduced for the 2006 model year.\n- The Ford Fusion is manufactured at Ford's Hermosillo Stamping & Assembly plant alongside the Lincoln MKZ and formerly the discontinued Mercury Milan, and all three shared the CD3 platform.\n- Patrick Carpentier competed part-time in the NASCAR Sprint Cup Series, driving the No. 32 Ford Fusion for Go FAS Racing.\n- Trevor Bayne competed full-time in the Monster Energy NASCAR Cup Series in the No. 6 Ford Fusion for Roush Fenway Racing and part-time in the NASCAR Xfinity Series in the No. 60 Ford Mustang for RFR.",
        "type": "TextSummary"
      },
      {
        "id": 1,
        "original_id": "32b51d9e-4de5-5666-ba10-8c7beda60ff4",
        "text": "Page: Patrick Carpentier. Sentence: Patrick Carpentier (born August 13, 1971) is a Canadian professional auto racing driver.\nPage: Patrick Carpentier. Sentence: He currently competes part-time in the NASCAR Sprint Cup Series, driving the No. 32 Ford Fusion for Go FAS Racing.\nPage: Ford Fusion (Americas). Sentence: Introduced for model year 2006, the Fusion is manufactured at Ford's Hermosillo Stamping & Assembly plant along with its rebadged variant the Lincoln MKZ — and formerly with its now discontinued rebadged variant, the Mercury Milan, all sharing the CD3 platform.\nPage: 1997 CART season. Sentence: Rookie of the Year was Patrick Carpentier.\nPage: Trevor Bayne. Sentence: He currently competes full-time in the Monster Energy NASCAR Cup Series, driving the No. 6 Ford Fusion for Roush Fenway Racing and part-time in the NASCAR Xfinity Series, driving the No. 60 Ford Mustang for RFR.",
